{
  "about": "Confluence Cloud pages read through its REST API; spaces listed, content found by CQL, one page read, the children of a page, folder, whiteboard, database or embed listed.",
  "base": "https://example.atlassian.net/wiki",
  "calls": [
    {
      "about": "List the spaces the account may see, 25 at a time. Answers each space's id, key, name, type and homepageId, the page children starts from. keys narrows it to spaces by key, as an address shows it (/spaces/ENG/...). When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value is the next call's cursor.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "spaces",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 500,
          "name": "keys",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/spaces",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "keys",
            "value": "{keys}"
          },
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Read one page by its id, which is in its address (/spaces/ENG/pages/123456/Title). Answers its title, status, spaceId, parentId, version and links, and its body in Confluence storage format, in body.storage.value, which is XHTML with Confluence's own tags and macros, markup and not text.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "id",
          "status",
          "title",
          "spaceId",
          "parentId",
          "parentType",
          "version",
          "body",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "page",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 20,
          "name": "id",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/pages/{id}",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "body-format",
            "value": "storage"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "List the direct children of a page, folder, whiteboard, database or embed, 25 at a time, in the order of the tree. Answers each child's id, title, status and type (page, folder, whiteboard, database or embed). To go down a level, give the child's id, and give its type with an s as kind. A child whose type is folder takes kind=folders. kind is one of pages (the default), folders, whiteboards, databases and embeds. When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value is the next call's cursor, with the same id and kind.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 65536,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "children",
      "params": [
        {
          "log": true,
          "max": 20,
          "name": "id",
          "pattern": "^[0-9]+$",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "default": "pages",
          "log": true,
          "name": "kind",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "enum",
          "values": [
            "pages",
            "folders",
            "whiteboards",
            "databases",
            "embeds"
          ]
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v2/{kind}/{id}/direct-children",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "about": "Find content by CQL, Confluence's query language, 25 at a time, as in type = page AND space = \"ENG\" AND title ~ \"runbook\". Answers each hit's id, type, status, title and _links.webui, which names its space. When more than limit follow, _links.next is in the answer, and its cursor= value, percent-decoded, is the next call's cursor.",
      "answer": {
        "max": 262144,
        "select": [
          "results",
          "size",
          "limit",
          "_links"
        ]
      },
      "kind": "read",
      "name": "search",
      "params": [
        {
          "max": 2000,
          "name": "cql",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "default": 25,
          "name": "limit",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "max": 1000,
          "name": "cursor",
          "optional": true,
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/rest/api/content/search",
        "query": [
          {
            "key": "cql",
            "value": "{cql}"
          },
          {
            "key": "limit",
            "value": "{limit}"
          },
          {
            "key": "cursor",
            "value": "{cursor}"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "check": "spaces",
  "credential": {
    "env": "CONFLUENCE_AUTH",
    "header": "Authorization: Basic {credential}",
    "mint": [
      "CONFLUENCE_EMAIL",
      "CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN"
    ],
    "mint_command": [
      "confluence/mint"
    ],
    "not_secret": [
      "CONFLUENCE_EMAIL"
    ]
  },
  "name": "confluence"
}
